#: ../../source/shelljs_README.md:217
msgid "pushd([options,] [dir | '-N' | '+N'])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/shelljs_README.md:221
msgid ""
"`-n`: Suppresses the normal change of directory when adding directories "
"to the stack, so that only the stack is manipulated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/shelljs_README.md:222 ../../source/shelljs_README.md:246
#: ../../source/shelljs_README.md:271
msgid "`-q`: Supresses output to the console."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/shelljs_README.md:224 ../../source/shelljs_README.md:248
#: ../../source/shelljs_README.md:273
msgid "Arguments:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/shelljs_README.md:226
msgid ""
"`dir`: Sets the current working directory to the top of the stack, then "
"executes the equivalent of `cd dir`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/shelljs_README.md:227
msgid ""
"`+N`: Brings the Nth directory (counting from the left of the list "
"printed by dirs, starting with zero) to the top of the list by rotating "
"the stack."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/shelljs_README.md:228
msgid ""
"`-N`: Brings the Nth directory (counting from the right of the list "
"printed by dirs, starting with zero) to the top of the list by rotating "
"the stack."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/shelljs_README.md:238
msgid ""
"Save the current directory on the top of the directory stack and then "
"`cd` to `dir`. With no arguments, `pushd` exchanges the top two "
"directories. Returns an array of paths in the stack."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/shelljs_README.md:241
msgid "popd([options,] ['-N' | '+N'])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/shelljs_README.md:245
msgid ""
"`-n`: Suppress the normal directory change when removing directories from"
" the stack, so that only the stack is manipulated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/shelljs_README.md:250
msgid ""
"`+N`: Removes the Nth directory (counting from the left of the list "
"printed by dirs), starting with zero."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/shelljs_README.md:251
msgid ""
"`-N`: Removes the Nth directory (counting from the right of the list "
"printed by dirs), starting with zero."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/shelljs_README.md:263
msgid ""
"When no arguments are given, `popd` removes the top directory from the "
"stack and performs a `cd` to the new top directory. The elements are "
"numbered from 0, starting at the first directory listed with dirs (i.e., "
"`popd` is equivalent to `popd +0`). Returns an array of paths in the "
"stack."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/shelljs_README.md:266
msgid "dirs([options | '+N' | '-N'])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/shelljs_README.md:270
msgid "`-c`: Clears the directory stack by deleting all of the elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/shelljs_README.md:275
msgid ""
"`+N`: Displays the Nth directory (counting from the left of the list "
"printed by dirs when invoked without options), starting with zero."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/shelljs_README.md:276
msgid ""
"`-N`: Displays the Nth directory (counting from the right of the list "
"printed by dirs when invoked without options), starting with zero."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/shelljs_README.md:278
msgid ""
"Display the list of currently remembered directories. Returns an array of"
" paths in the stack, or a single path if `+N` or `-N` was specified."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/shelljs_README.md:280
msgid "See also: `pushd`, `popd`"
msgstr ""

