"Evaluates `expression` using the available primaries and returns "
"corresponding value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/shelljs_README.md:617
msgid "ShellString.prototype.to(file)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/shelljs_README.md:625
msgid ""
"Analogous to the redirection operator `>` in Unix, but works with "
"`ShellStrings` (such as those returned by `cat`, `grep`, etc.). _Like "
"Unix redirections, `to()` will overwrite any existing file!_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/shelljs_README.md:630
msgid "ShellString.prototype.toEnd(file)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/shelljs_README.md:638
msgid ""
"Analogous to the redirect-and-append operator `>>` in Unix, but works "
"with `ShellStrings` (such as those returned by `cat`, `grep`, etc.)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/shelljs_README.md:642
msgid "touch([options,] file [, file ...])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/shelljs_README.md:643
msgid "touch([options,] file_array)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/shelljs_README.md:647
msgid "`-a`: Change only the access time"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/shelljs_README.md:648
msgid "`-c`: Do not create any files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/shelljs_README.md:649
msgid "`-m`: Change only the modification time"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/shelljs_README.md:650
msgid "`-d DATE`: Parse `DATE` and use it instead of current time"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/shelljs_README.md:651
msgid "`-r FILE`: Use `FILE`'s times instead of current time"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/shelljs_README.md:661
msgid ""
"Update the access and modification times of each `FILE` to the current "
"time. A `FILE` argument that does not exist is created empty, unless `-c`"
" is supplied. This is a partial implementation of "
"[`touch(1)`](http://linux.die.net/man/1/touch)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/shelljs_README.md:666
msgid "uniq([options,] [input, [output]])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/shelljs_README.md:670
msgid "`-i`: Ignore case while comparing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/shelljs_README.md:671
msgid "`-c`: Prefix lines by the number of occurrences"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/shelljs_README.md:672
msgid "`-d`: Only print duplicate lines, one for each group of identical lines"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/shelljs_README.md:682
msgid "Filter adjacent matching lines from `input`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/shelljs_README.md:685
msgid "which(command)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/shelljs_README.md:693
msgid ""
"Searches for `command` in the system's `PATH`. On Windows, this uses the "
"`PATHEXT` variable to append the extension if it's not already "
"executable. Returns string containing the absolute path to `command`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/shelljs_README.md:698
msgid "exit(code)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/shelljs_README.md:700
msgid "Exits the current process with the given exit `code`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/shelljs_README.md:702
msgid "error()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/shelljs_README.md:704
msgid ""
"Tests if error occurred in the last command. Returns a truthy value if an"
" error returned, or a falsy value otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/shelljs_README.md:707
msgid ""
"**Note**: do not rely on the return value to be an error message. If you "
"need the last error message, use the `.stderr` attribute from the last "
"command's return value instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/shelljs_README.md:712
msgid "ShellString(str)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/shelljs_README.md:720
msgid ""
"Turns a regular string into a string-like object similar to what each "
"command returns. This has special methods, like `.to()` and `.toEnd()`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/shelljs_README.md:724
msgid "env['VAR_NAME']"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/shelljs_README.md:726
msgid ""
"Object containing environment variables (both getter and setter). "
"Shortcut to `process.env`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/shelljs_README.md:729
msgid "Pipes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/shelljs_README.md:739
msgid ""
"Commands can send their output to another command in a pipe-like fashion."
" `sed`, `grep`, `cat`, `exec`, `to`, and `toEnd` can appear on the right-"
"hand side of a pipe. Pipes can be chained."
msgstr ""

